{title: Resurrecting (FJ_146_en)}
{subtitle: Auferstehen}
{song_number: 146}
{language: en}
{tempo: 74}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
The head that [F]once was crowned [Am]with [G]thorns is crowned with [F]glory [C]now.
The Saviour [F]knelt to [Am]wash our [G]feet; now at his [F]feet we [C]bow.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
The one who [F]wore our [Am]sin and [G]shame now robed in [F]majes[C]ty.
The radiance [F]of [Am]perfect [G]love now shines for [F]all to [C]see.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
The fear that [F]held us [Am]now gives [G]way to Him who [F]is our [C]peace.
His final [F]breath up[Am]on the [G]cross is now a[F]live in [C]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F]Your name, Your [C]name is [G]victory. [F]All praise will [C]rise to [G]Christ our King.
[F]Your name, Your [C]name is [G]victory. [F]All praise will [C]rise to [G]Christ our King. [C]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
[F]By Your [C]spirit I will [G]rise from the ashes of [C/E]defeat.
The [F]resurrected [Csus4]King is resur[G]recting me.
[F]In Your [C]name I come a[G]live to declare Your [C/E]victory.
The [F]resurrected [Csus4]King is resur[G]recting me. [F]
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: 4}
The [F]tomb where soldiers [Am]watched in [G]vain was borrowed [F]for three [C]days.
His body [F]there would [Am]not re[G]main. Our God has [F]robbed the [C]grave.
Our God has [F]robbed the [C]grave.
{end_of_verse}
